    ==================================================[bold]
                                             STATION GOAL[/bold]
    ==================================================[bold]
    The goal of the { $station } shift is to keep the station operational.[/bold]

    Your station must remain operational for at least 2 hours.

    Once the minimum time has passed, you are entitled to call the evacuation shuttle.
    You may also end the shift early by completing the secondary objective [bold]if the crew wishes[/bold].

    Completing the primary [bold]or[/bold] the secondary goal earns you your full salary, but no bonuses.
    Completing the primary [bold]and[/bold] the secondary goal earns you your full salary and bonuses.
station-goal-end =
    Glory to NanoTrasen!
    ==================================================[italic]
                                          Place for stamps[/italic]
station-goal-singularity =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: build a singularity-based generator.[/bold]

    All parts for the goal must be ordered or made on the station. Using the containment field generators or components already present on the station is strictly prohibited.

    To complete the goal, the singularity must be started.

    At the end of the shift the whole structure will be detached from the station and transported to another facility.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-solar-panels =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: build a solar panel network.[/bold]

    Requirements:
    - The network must have at least two branches, placed on opposite ends of the station.
    - Each branch must have at least 36 solar panels.
    - Each branch must have at least two SMESes that are not connected to the station.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-artifacts =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: find and research artifacts.[/bold]

    The station crew must find at least two artifacts by any means other than buying them.

    Science staff must research the artifacts found and document their properties.

    Accepted documentation is a report for every node (printed on the dedicated console) and a separate document describing the artifact's structure in plain words.

    Every document must be stamped by the research director or the captain. The artifacts and their documentation must be delivered to the Central Command station.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-bank =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: build an orbital vault with supplies and technology.[/bold]

    The vault must be placed in space, apart from the main station, protected from meteors, and have its own power supply.

    The vault must contain at least four crates:
    - a crate of advanced medicine;
    - a crate of the best seeds;
    - a freezer crate of highly nutritious food;
    - a crate of valuable but not unique circuit boards.

    Notes:
    Every medicine must be provided in at least 100u, poured into sterile chemical containers or packed as medipens.

    The medicine crate must contain at least fifteen different medicines, or ten medicines if at least fifty medical threads, regenerative meshes and blood packs each are added.

    Recommended medicines:
    1. arithrazine / ultravasculine;
    2. bicaridine / polypyrylium oligomers;
    3. dexalin plus;
    4. dermaline;
    5. diphenhydramine / stelloxadone;
    6. doxarubixadone;
    7. cryoxadone;
    8. leporazine;
    9. oculine;
    10. pyrazine;
    11. sigynate / siderlac;
    12. tricordrazine / omnizine;
    13. charcoal;
    14. phalanximine;
    15. epinephrine.

    The chief medical officer may change the list with the captain's approval.

    The best seeds must be selected and bred by the botanists.

    The food is prepared by the chefs at their discretion.

    The science circuit boards must be unique and made with at least ten units of gold, silver or uranium.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-zoo =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: improve recreation for the station staff.[/bold]

    Engineering must build a zoo with at least 3 (three) enclosures, one species per enclosure. Every enclosure must be supplied with food for its species and a cleaning robot. Each enclosure must be at least 16 m².

    The animals must be ordered through cargo.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-mining-outpost =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: build an orbital mining outpost.[/bold]

    The outpost must be placed in space, apart from the main station, protected from meteors, and have its own power supply, gravity and atmosphere.

    The outpost must have at least two living rooms with lights and windows. Work equipment: at least two pickaxes and two ore bags, and at least two mining hardsuits.

    The outpost must have a storage room for the mined resources and supplies: at least 500u (five hundred units) of beer in a snack freezer crate, and at least four kits each for brute and burn damage.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-tesla =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: build a tesla-based generator.[/bold]

    All parts for the goal must be ordered or made on the station. Using the containment field generators or components already present on the station is strictly prohibited.

    To complete the goal, the tesla must be started.

    At the end of the shift the whole structure will be detached from the station and transported to another facility.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-security =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: build and supply a training complex for Security, then test the staff.[/bold]
    This station will later be redeployed to a sector bordering an unsafe one.

    Engineering must build a training complex in the form of an obstacle course. An average trained officer should need about 30 seconds to complete it.
    The course must include:
    - Winding glass corridors.
    - Various obstacles to climb over.
    - A wooden building with targets, simulating the capture of a random department.
    Engineering may build other safe kinds of obstacles as well.

    Medical must make a batch of at least 12 ephedrine pills, 20u each, and hand them over to the warden for storage in a secure container.

    Security must run every member of the department through the course and record the results in writing. The results must state the officer's full name and the time it took them to complete the course. The best officers will get a chance at a contract for the next shift on this station. Every officer's result must be included in the goal status report.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-shuttle-med =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: build a crewed medical shuttle.[/bold]

    The shuttle must meet the following requirements:
    1. A stable power supply and a backup SMES.
    2. It must be able to roll, pitch and yaw.
    3. Equipment inside the compartments must be easy to access.
    4. A chemistry section with the matching equipment for at least one staff member.
    5. A compartment with medical beds for at least ten people.
    6. A compartment with medicine and food supplies, and a crate of body bags.

    Reference for unqualified staff:
    Roll: rotation.
    Pitch: moving forward and backward.
    Yaw: moving sideways.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-shuttle-sec =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: build a crewed assault shuttle.[/bold]

    The shuttle must meet the following requirements:
    1. A stable power supply and a backup SMES.
    2. It must be able to roll, pitch and yaw.
    3. Equipment inside the compartments must be easy to access.
    4. Seats and gear for at least five security officers.
    Each officer's gear must include at least one legal firearm not taken from the armory, an armor vest, a helmet and a uniform.
    5. A compartment with medicine and food supplies for at least five people.

    Reference for unqualified staff:
    Roll: rotation.
    Pitch: moving forward and backward.
    Yaw: moving sideways.

    { station-goal-end }
