station-goal-theatre =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: build a theatre area.[/bold]
    Negotiations with major companies on partnership agreements will be held on this station. A warm welcome for the guests is important.

    The theatre area must include:
    1. A stage of at least 28 m².
    2. Seating for at least 21 people, including separate seats fitted for Vox.
    3. A backstage area with various outfits, musical instruments, several crates of toys and an H.O.N.K. mech.
    4. A room or rooms for four actors, with five pies of any kind per actor.

    The materials for the clown suits can be found in the theatrical performances crate.
    If a test performance is held, the station's service department will be rewarded on arrival at the Central Command station.
    Once the work is done, Central Command may send a representative to attend a test performance.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-ai =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: build a self-sufficient AI module.[/bold]
    Once built, the module must be undocked from the station and left to drift in space.

    Requirements:
    1. Self-sufficient power from solar panels or an RTG, connected to an SMES and a substation.
    2. A compartment for an active positronic brain.
    3. A mass scanner console.
    4. Two cyborgs with inactive positronic brains: one engineering and one science.
    5. An airlock into the module with command access.
    6. A communications server and a wired camera router.
    7. A cooling loop around the outside of the module.
    The cooling loop must be a channel at least one meter wide, fully filled with any gas except the regular air mix, colder than -100 degrees Celsius and at a pressure at least 3 times the standard atmospheric pressure. The loop must surround at least 80% of the module.

    Additional safety measures are recommended:
    - Meteor protection.
    - A high-voltage grille around the module.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-botany =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: build greenhouses and breed temperature-adapted plants.[/bold]

    Three climate-controlled compartments must be built on or near the station:
    - A compartment at 5 degrees Celsius.
    - A compartment at 25 degrees Celsius.
    - A compartment at 45 degrees Celsius.

    Each compartment must have at least six hydroponics trays and a full water tank.
    Each compartment must contain at least one plant adapted to its temperature.
    To speed things up, pouring 10u–20u of unstable mutagen into the hydroponics trays is recommended.

    { station-goal-end }
station-goal-bunker =
    { station-goal-start }[bold]

    Secondary goal: prepare the station for powerful hyperenergetic flows.[/bold]

    Security, Medical and Command each need an extra room, hereafter called a "bunker", where the station crew can shelter from the effects of hyperenergetic flows.

    General bunker requirements:
    1. At least 25 m².
    2. Reinforced walls.
    3. Entry through two opaque airlocks with the matching department access.
    4. At least four pilot seats.
    5. Basic medicine in pill form with a note on its use, and brute damage kits.
    6. Food supplies for four people for at least 72 hours.
    7. Self-sufficient power, plus air and oxygen canisters.
    8. Lockers with bio and radiation protection gear, as well as emergency EVA suits and a bomb suit.

    The Security bunker must also include two Enforcers and three lethal shotgun shell dispensers.
    The Medical bunker must also have a defibrillator and a battery charger.

    { station-goal-end }
